    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Miguel Vargas** and **Kyle Tucker**. **Miguel Vargas** earns our top score of 63.96, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against the 5.02 xERA of Andrew Abbott. The combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s environment and his slot in the three-hole makes him our most bankable asset. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (60.91) remains a primary focal point; despite a moderate SP skill rating from Shane Drohan, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base projections and order placement sustain his strong start status. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.18) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.31) are solid tertiary options, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** notably enjoying a 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages, which helps mitigate the threat of Logan Gilbert on the mound.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the bottom of the order, where **Wade Meckler** (38.70) fell just short of the starting threshold. While **Wade Meckler** offered an enticing 10% boost for occupying the leadoff spot, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a high-risk matchup against Jacob deGrom, whose 3.13 xERA serves as a significant deterrent. Elsewhere, we are navigating a quieter day for the bench; stalwarts like **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined by scheduled off-days, and **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, limiting our late-game versatility. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Andy Pages**, as his lineup position is still pending; if he drops out of the two-hole, his marginal score of 55.50 could be subject to further volatility.",
